Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 19:58:44 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] qcom: import DMA-BUFs for from_blob on MSM DRM

MSM DRM can't map host pointers, so Tensor.from_blob takes the DMA-BUF fd behind
the pointer and QCOM imports and binds that instead. KGSL keeps mapping the
pointer. openpilot uses this to run models on camera frames without a copy.

Freeing an external buffer now calls the allocator's _free_external, a no-op by
default. QCOM uses it to unbind the import or unmap the KGSL user memory mapping,
which were kept until the process exited.
