From c9eb210f5d2dd74ac02880407454f68d87f66050 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeebshihadeh@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 05:18:27 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] qcom: pick the kernel interface of a graph's submit at
 run time

A pickled graph had its submit ioctl, and the request it passes, built for the
kernel interface of the device it was compiled on, so models compiled on the
upstream kernel (MSM DRM) couldn't run on the downstream one (KGSL), or the
other way. One openpilot release has to run on both kernels for a while, and
releases are built on one device.

The rest of the graph is the same on both: the Adreno programs and command
stream don't depend on the kernel. So submit now builds both requests in one
buffer, KGSL's at 0 and MSM's after it, and a third variable bound by the
device (qcom_msm) picks the ioctl and the request at run time, next to the
fd and context. Checked by saving a TinyJit graph on each kernel and loading
it on the other (5 runs match the reference both ways).

When KGSL goes, the KGSL request and the qcom_msm variable go with it.
